Ja, looking at Hamin... Say Yejun's the one
who keeps everyone in line.

00:49:25.460 --> 00:49:29.660
Then Hamin... how do I say this?
[Chat: He'll guess down to the centimeter.]

00:49:29.670 --> 00:49:39.800
He seems steady. Like he'd stick to his guns,
but he's got a thoughtful side too.

00:49:39.810 --> 00:49:48.520
They've all got their own thing going.
A mix of qualities, I guess?

00:49:48.980 --> 00:49:57.720
Steady, because everybody here has
such a strong personality. In the middle...

00:49:59.080 --> 00:50:05.370
Hang on.

00:50:05.380 --> 00:50:12.900
They really stand out. Look at their hair,
their eye colors, all that. But Hamin...

00:50:12.910 --> 00:50:16.140
He's steady. Less is more, you know?

00:50:16.150 --> 00:50:23.140
So he can fit with a lot of different styles
and it wouldn't feel out of place.

00:50:25.860 --> 00:50:29.560
This is hard to put into words. Hamin...

00:50:29.570 --> 00:50:37.760
Put him with anyone
and I think they'd have good chemistry.

00:50:37.770 --> 00:50:45.300
I mean, I'm sure there's a name
for each pairing in the group.

00:50:45.310 --> 00:50:50.260
But I feel like Hamin would work
with any of them.

00:50:51.900 --> 00:50:56.960
He doesn't need to stand out on his own.
It's more like they click. What's the word?

00:51:00.260 --> 00:51:07.560
Uh... I think he makes it easier
for everyone to gel.

00:51:10.040 --> 00:51:17.880
He might look standoffish at first,
but he seems easygoing. Easygoing.

00:51:20.440 --> 00:51:28.340
And by easygoing, I mean
he's still got his own convictions.

00:51:30.100 --> 00:51:36.940
But I bet he's good at adapting.
He'd back up the others instead of showing off.

00:51:36.950 --> 00:51:40.770
Like he's the secret ingredient.
That's kind of his role.

00:51:40.780 --> 00:51:43.280
[Chat: Are you a member? LOL]

00:51:45.580 --> 00:51:51.220
He supports them, but that doesn't mean
he just fades into the background.

00:51:52.900 --> 00:51:57.990
No. It's more like
he brings out the chemistry.

00:51:58.000 --> 00:52:00.400
[Chat: Did you watch their videos first? LOL]

00:52:00.410 --> 00:52:09.980
No, I seriously didn't watch their videos.
I was saving my first taste for someday.

00:52:09.990 --> 00:52:16.440
I know they do livestreams and stuff.
I just didn't watch them.

00:52:17.240 --> 00:52:19.260
[Reading chat] “Hamin's role?”
Right.

00:52:21.220 --> 00:52:27.120
For his role... well, first off...

00:52:28.340 --> 00:52:36.880
Sorry, but I bet he's got an amazing voice.
I haven't called anyone a standout vocalist yet.

00:52:36.890 --> 00:52:39.540
An incredible singer and a good dancer.

00:52:41.300 --> 00:52:44.680
Man, this is going to be fun.

00:52:48.120 --> 00:52:54.840
He feels like... white. White?
Yeah, that's the vibe.

00:52:55.120 --> 00:52:58.860
He gives off best-vocalist vibes.
That's my impression.

00:52:58.870 --> 00:53:02.820
A white Doberman. That's it.

00:53:03.860 --> 00:53:15.180
He seems like he loves PLAVE as a group
more than anyone.

00:53:15.190 --> 00:53:17.870
[Chat: Singing AND dancing?
That's overpowered.]

00:53:17.880 --> 00:53:23.340
Dobermans are loyal, right?
He seems loyal in a protective way.

00:53:23.350 --> 00:53:27.520
Oh, hi, Roda!

00:53:30.560 --> 00:53:34.840
Looking at him, that's exactly it.
Though with Hamin...

00:53:34.850 --> 00:53:41.040
I feel like all I've said is “solid support.”
Even I think that's a little unsatisfying.

00:53:43.800 --> 00:53:48.040
You want me to guess their animal symbols?
They have animal symbols?

00:53:49.720 --> 00:53:50.700
Huh? Hamin...

00:53:53.380 --> 00:53:59.480
Just going off their looks,
Noah...

00:53:59.490 --> 00:54:01.150
[Chat: Good instincts or not?]

00:54:01.160 --> 00:54:05.100
gives me Pegasus vibes.

00:54:07.320 --> 00:54:10.300
Doesn't Bamby already have
the whole Bambi thing?

00:54:14.560 --> 00:54:16.400
They have official animals?

00:54:17.340 --> 00:54:19.840
Hi! Welcome back. It's been a while.

00:54:19.850 --> 00:54:28.760
Hamin... a black horse?
Or a crow?

00:54:29.740 --> 00:54:31.280
I doubt they'd pick a crow.

00:54:32.940 --> 00:54:35.780
[Reading chat] “How princely is he
if you went with Pegasus?”

00:54:35.790 --> 00:54:39.840
Black horse, crow, Doberman.
That's the vibe I get.

00:54:43.320 --> 00:54:49.440
And Yejun. He's totally a border collie to me,
but you said they have animal symbols...

00:54:50.900 --> 00:54:52.680
An animal symbol.

00:54:55.500 --> 00:54:58.840
That's cool. Did you know crows
are really smart?

00:55:02.420 --> 00:55:04.680
But I doubt that's what they'd pick.

00:55:06.800 --> 00:55:16.060
I can't get border collie out of my head
for Yejun. But it's not a border collie, right?

00:55:16.070 --> 00:55:19.330
[Chat: Look at our usernames for a clue.]

00:55:19.340 --> 00:55:21.040
It's not a border collie, is it?

00:55:22.320 --> 00:55:28.900
Yejun... Hamin... Yejun.
Something blue. Like something blue-backed...

00:55:28.910 --> 00:55:32.180
White... It can't be a mackerel, right?

00:55:33.340 --> 00:55:37.060
A dolphin? Oh!
He does have a dolphin vibe, too.

00:55:37.070 --> 00:55:42.160
Huh? It could still be a border collie.
It's in your username?

00:55:43.320 --> 00:55:44.920
Wait, there's a dolphin?

00:55:45.600 --> 00:55:50.940
Huh? Really?
Then I think Yejun's a dolphin.

00:55:52.600 --> 00:55:53.400
Dolphin.

00:55:54.900 --> 00:55:58.580
I was thinking along the lines
of a blue-backed fish, and dolphin came to mind.

00:56:00.060 --> 00:56:01.720
Keep border collie on the list.

00:56:03.380 --> 00:56:07.840
Hang on. Pegasus.
Noah: Pegasus. Final answer.

00:56:07.850 --> 00:56:11.540
How did I get to blue-backed fish?
Well, he's kind of blue here.

00:56:11.550 --> 00:56:14.180
Oh, I missed the hint in chat just now.

00:56:17.020 --> 00:56:21.360
For Bamby, isn't there an animal called Bambi?
It fits his look, too.

00:56:22.320 --> 00:56:25.180
Is Bamby's animal maybe Bambi?

00:56:26.980 --> 00:56:32.660
Pink Chihuahua, little mutt.
He's the GOAT of being cute.

00:56:32.670 --> 00:56:38.420
Wait, is it not a bambi?
Is there an animal called a dambi?

00:56:39.680 --> 00:56:42.400
Isn't a bambi a kind of deer?

00:56:46.960 --> 00:56:48.260
Is it Bambi?

00:56:49.780 --> 00:56:51.600
Bambi is a character?

00:56:52.680 --> 00:56:54.760
Then I'll go with spotted deer.

00:56:55.000 --> 00:56:58.650
[Chat: Wait till you find out Noah's animal.
You might be disappointed.]

00:56:59.780 --> 00:57:02.440
I'm putting down spotted deer.

00:57:04.040 --> 00:57:06.440
You're saying Pegasus is a pretty good guess?

00:57:06.450 --> 00:57:16.680
Then maybe Pegasus or a unicorn.
Something like that.

00:57:19.200 --> 00:57:21.600
Eunho's definitely a wolf.

00:57:27.500 --> 00:57:31.220
Should I think about yours a little more?
If not a wolf, what else could it be?

00:57:31.230 --> 00:57:41.620
Ah, he's a wolf. A wolf.
Definitely a wolf.

00:57:43.180 --> 00:57:49.840
Hamin: black horse... No, Doberman is right.
He's got that Doberman look.

00:57:50.560 --> 00:57:52.780
I don't think it's a crow.

00:57:52.790 --> 00:57:55.200
[Chat: Well, it does have four legs. LOL]

00:57:56.900 --> 00:58:01.980
I feel like the fans would go, “What?
A crow?!” and scold me. Pass.

00:58:11.820 --> 00:58:15.440
There's a Dolphin Duo? Wait,
does that make this one an orca?

00:58:17.420 --> 00:58:19.840
If there's a Dolphin Duo... an orca?

00:58:22.420 --> 00:58:31.100
He seems like someone
who sticks to his own opinions. Am I right?

00:58:34.620 --> 00:58:43.060
Those two seem like they'd really click.
Yejun and Hamin, right?

00:58:43.320 --> 00:58:45.860
[Reading chat] “Why are you so nervous?”

00:58:45.870 --> 00:58:47.900
You all just love to tease me.

00:58:47.940 --> 00:58:53.120
Ah, but now I want to know too!
You got me curious.

00:58:54.220 --> 00:58:59.320
I think that's enough for now.
I've got more to taste, after all.

00:59:00.820 --> 00:59:05.640
So... aha. Now I'm curious too.

00:59:07.460 --> 00:59:12.700
Ja, let's leave it there
and see what else we've got.

00:59:12.710 --> 00:59:14.820
Oh, hey, I need to look at this.

00:59:14.830 --> 00:59:16.950
[Chat: Time to grade your guesses!]

00:59:16.960 --> 00:59:19.550
[Reading chat] “Two wrong, three right?”

00:59:22.480 --> 00:59:26.540
Yejun. “Producer”? Wait, what?

00:59:30.880 --> 00:59:32.640
Leader! Ah!

00:59:32.650 --> 00:59:34.730
[Chat: Everyone, grab a stick! LOL]

00:59:34.740 --> 00:59:39.900
He keeps the team in line! I said “a leader who
isn't the leader.” He really IS the leader!

00:59:42.260 --> 00:59:43.180
Leader.

00:59:45.900 --> 00:59:53.260
Hang on. You're saying he's the leader,
a main vocalist, AND a producer?

00:59:55.000 --> 00:59:58.260
They write and compose
their own songs?

00:59:58.270 --> 01:00:03.440
No, but seriously... that's fucking cool.

01:00:04.000 --> 01:00:07.710
[Chat: Producers write, compose, arrange,
and direct recording sessions.]

01:00:07.720 --> 01:00:15.300
He does everything. And he's not
the only one who does everything?

01:00:16.200 --> 01:00:19.080
Ah, “maebo.” Main vocalist.

01:00:21.620 --> 01:00:25.040
Noah. Ja, the first prince.

01:00:25.050 --> 01:00:27.240
I said that. It's not on the screen.

01:00:27.250 --> 01:00:34.920
Main vocalist. I said he could rap and sing.
Or rather, sing and rap. Right?

01:00:37.980 --> 01:00:42.400
So main vocalist and producing too.

01:00:42.410 --> 01:00:46.080
Wait, can he rap too?
He seems like he'd be good at everything.

01:00:46.090 --> 01:00:47.020
[Chat: He can!]

01:00:47.030 --> 01:00:50.840
Ja. Oh, dancer.

01:00:50.850 --> 01:00:54.550
[On screen: Bamby — main dancer,
vocals, choreographer]

01:00:54.560 --> 01:00:58.040
That's insane. That's insane.

01:00:59.740 --> 01:01:03.360
Vocals AND choreography?

01:01:05.660 --> 01:01:07.060
A choreographer?

01:01:09.060 --> 01:01:14.180
I said he gave off dancer vibes.
I didn't get as far as choreographer.

01:01:16.860 --> 01:01:19.660
Wait, I got that right!

01:01:19.900 --> 01:01:22.720
What the hell? I forgot I'd even said that.

01:01:22.730 --> 01:01:25.960
[Highlighted note: Total dancer energy
+ stronger on vocals]

01:01:25.970 --> 01:01:27.530
[Chat: He hits high notes too.]

01:01:27.540 --> 01:01:32.660
No way. But I did think
he'd be a good dancer.

01:01:32.670 --> 01:01:38.480
Like, clothes flying, hitting each beat.
That K-pop idol precision.

01:01:38.490 --> 01:01:44.560
I could picture those sharp stops.
Really clean, controlled moves.

01:01:44.570 --> 01:01:45.610
[Chat: Nailed Bamby.]

01:01:45.620 --> 01:01:52.200
I figured he'd be good, but he went
from dancer to choreographer.

01:01:52.210 --> 01:01:55.860
Not just the main dancer. A choreographer!
His lines really are beautiful.

01:01:55.870 --> 01:02:02.480
If I get the chance, I should do a stream
where I learn PLAVE choreography.

01:02:02.490 --> 01:02:07.500
Ja, Eunho. Main rapper. Main rapper.

01:02:08.820 --> 01:02:13.240
Vocals and producer. Wow. Come on.

01:02:15.320 --> 01:02:16.080
That's insane.

01:02:18.000 --> 01:02:20.860
Imagine how much feedback
they trade while producing.

01:02:22.180 --> 01:02:24.460
Vocals... no, rapper, right.

01:02:25.500 --> 01:02:29.820
Did I not say it here? Oh, I did:
“main dancer, rapper.” Right.

01:02:31.100 --> 01:02:39.820
I really thought he'd be good.
Eunho just looked the part. I get it.

01:02:41.200 --> 01:02:46.080
I had heard that they do their own production.

01:02:46.090 --> 01:02:50.420
Why? My older sister is a huge PLAVE fan.

01:02:53.400 --> 01:02:58.980
She kept telling me, “Try them on stream.”
Then, “Make a whole meal of it on stream.”

01:03:00.340 --> 01:03:03.560
That's what she'd tell me. She's over there.

01:03:03.570 --> 01:03:09.340
Yejun, Noah, and Eunho make the music,
and Bamby and Hamin make the dances? Solid.

01:03:12.740 --> 01:03:20.240
But I really didn't watch their content. Even
when she'd tell me stuff, I tried not to listen.

01:03:20.250 --> 01:03:23.460
Why? It wouldn't be as fun
when I finally dug in like this.

01:03:23.470 --> 01:03:29.980
So I avoided whatever I could.
I knew I'd get around to it someday.

01:03:29.990 --> 01:03:35.320
Ja, main dancer. Ooh, lead rapper.

01:03:35.330 --> 01:03:38.720
Those roles are cool. Choreographer?

01:03:38.730 --> 01:03:40.530
[On screen: Hamin]

01:03:40.540 --> 01:03:41.820
Another choreographer?

01:03:41.830 --> 01:03:45.310
[Chat: The swimming guess gave me chills.]

01:03:45.320 --> 01:03:49.100
My swimming guess gave you chills?

01:03:52.820 --> 01:03:54.760
Eunho's good at swimming?

01:03:56.420 --> 01:04:01.140
[Reading chat] “Blood relatives don't listen.”
True. Neither me nor my sister listens.

01:04:03.680 --> 01:04:09.790
We give each other unsolicited life advice,
and neither of us takes it.

01:04:09.799 --> 01:04:15.720
“Uh-huh. Sure. Got it.”
Even this Chuseok it was like that.

01:04:18.480 --> 01:04:20.500
Yeah, exactly.

01:04:20.510 --> 01:04:23.590
[Chat: My little sibling ignores
my PLAVE pitches too.]

01:04:25.359 --> 01:04:29.500
I thought it'd be fun to get into them
for the first time with you all on stream.

01:04:29.520 --> 01:04:33.520
Huh, now I'm suddenly curious. Ja, so...

01:04:34.460 --> 01:04:38.560
Hang on. Let's crop off the side here.

01:04:40.140 --> 01:04:41.460
I'll zoom in on this part.

01:04:58.000 --> 01:05:01.390
They mentioned it in their introductions?

01:05:01.400 --> 01:05:03.400
There. “Member chemistry.”

01:05:05.580 --> 01:05:06.700
Oh!

01:05:09.540 --> 01:05:13.380
Let's make it easier to see.

01:05:15.200 --> 01:05:21.200
Whoa, there are a lot. This is fun.
Where's the Dolphin Duo?

01:05:25.400 --> 01:05:27.800
Ja... oh, the oldest-member duo.

01:05:27.810 --> 01:05:29.610
[On screen: Yejun & Noah]

01:05:29.620 --> 01:05:32.860
Berry Duo. This is fun.
[On screen: Yejun & Bamby]

01:05:33.480 --> 01:05:37.300
Puppy Duo. Yejun and Eunho.

01:05:37.310 --> 01:05:41.860
Oh, the border collie meets the wolf.

01:05:41.870 --> 01:05:44.740
I guessed the animals...
[Reading chat] “No Dolphin Duo?”

01:05:45.440 --> 01:05:48.380
Aw, too bad. What is the Dolphin Duo, then?

01:05:51.640 --> 01:05:57.180
Ye Line. Ye Line is Yejun and Hamin.

01:05:57.190 --> 01:06:01.620
Oh, is it Ye Line because Hamin's
on Yejun's side?

01:06:02.260 --> 01:06:07.020
Noah's Line. Pretty Line.
Oh, is it “pretty”?

01:06:09.800 --> 01:06:16.920
Oh, that's right? Ah, Yejun's line.
Then there's a bit of a rivalry, huh?

01:06:16.930 --> 01:06:18.600
Eunho and Noah are Noah's Line.

01:06:23.500 --> 01:06:33.660
So Bamby's caught in the middle. Two against
two, and he's the one who gets squished.

01:06:33.670 --> 01:06:37.840
Is “Pretty Line” a thing too?

01:06:40.460 --> 01:06:43.400
Oh, so to balance them out, there's Bam Line.

01:06:44.740 --> 01:06:47.200
Oh! That's hilarious.

01:06:50.520 --> 01:06:51.420
“Traits”...

01:06:54.200 --> 01:06:58.840
Bam Line is just Bamby?
So he's right in the middle.

01:06:58.850 --> 01:07:00.780
Yataz?

01:07:00.790 --> 01:07:07.060
There's so much to read here.

01:07:07.070 --> 01:07:13.640
Yataz, Noah's Line, Puppy Duo, Dance Duo.
Oh, Bamby and Hamin.

01:07:15.420 --> 01:07:21.280
Bamby wants PLLI to be in Bam Line?
That would be so reassuring.

01:07:21.290 --> 01:07:24.800
[Chat: Yataz comes from “Hey! Hop on!”
in the motorcycle MV scene.]

01:07:25.760 --> 01:07:30.980
Oh, Yataz is from riding a motorcycle
in the MV. [On screen: Bamby & Eunho]

01:07:30.990 --> 01:07:34.480
Now I want to see that music video.

01:07:35.280 --> 01:07:38.340
Yataz... what even is that?

01:07:39.280 --> 01:07:45.940
I fucking love that. I really do.
Yataz.

01:07:45.950 --> 01:07:50.040
Man, that really got me just now.

01:07:55.000 --> 01:07:56.850
Oh, the music's too loud, right?

01:07:59.140 --> 01:08:00.900
PLAVE's official logo.

01:08:08.940 --> 01:08:10.450
Oh, wow.

01:08:11.339 --> 01:08:12.559
That's so cool.

01:08:13.960 --> 01:08:16.550
Wow, look at the songs. Right, The 6th Summer…

01:08:16.560 --> 01:08:19.189
and Wait for you. Oh, and WAY 4 LUV.

01:08:19.199 --> 01:08:20.518
I like that one too.

01:08:20.519 --> 01:08:22.149
I think those are the three

01:08:22.159 --> 01:08:24.558
I've listened to the most.

01:08:24.559 --> 01:08:26.401
Out of the ones I've heard, anyway.

01:08:28.760 --> 01:08:30.350
Oh, Why? Why? Why?

01:08:31.599 --> 01:08:34.079
It's so good. It keeps popping

01:08:34.080 --> 01:08:37.378
into my head. Completely out of nowhere.

01:08:37.379 --> 01:08:39.990
It's weird. Three weeks, two months

01:08:40.000 --> 01:08:41.789
go by, and then I'll be on my own,

01:08:43.359 --> 01:08:44.950
just humming it. [Hums]

01:08:44.960 --> 01:08:48.039
It's ridiculously catchy.

01:08:48.040 --> 01:08:50.870
I haven't even listened to it that much.

01:08:50.880 --> 01:08:54.349
Then out of nowhere, there I go again.

01:08:54.359 --> 01:08:56.269
How do I put this?

01:08:56.279 --> 01:08:58.358
The way I'd describe this song…

01:08:58.359 --> 01:09:01.118
and this is just me, very personally…

01:09:01.119 --> 01:09:04.119
it's like Snowing Cheese chicken.

01:09:04.120 --> 01:09:05.298
That's how I describe it.

01:09:05.299 --> 01:09:07.658
Snowing Cheese chicken. Nene Chicken

01:09:07.659 --> 01:09:10.539
has this flavor. That's exactly what it's like.

01:09:10.640 --> 01:09:13.458
The first time I tried it, I was like,

01:09:13.459 --> 01:09:15.309
“What even is this flavor?”

01:09:15.319 --> 01:09:17.189
Then a month later, out of nowhere:

01:09:17.199 --> 01:09:19.158
“Man, I could go for Snowing Chicken.”

01:09:19.159 --> 01:09:20.896
That's exactly what this is like.

01:09:21.019 --> 01:09:23.039
[Reading chat] “Any you don't know?”

01:09:23.040 --> 01:09:25.070
I don't usually pick songs by title.

01:09:25.080 --> 01:09:26.718
I just put on a playlist.

01:09:26.719 --> 01:09:28.669
There's a lot of J-pop in the mix,

01:09:28.679 --> 01:09:31.358
and in the middle of all that,

01:09:31.359 --> 01:09:32.918
a PLAVE song will come on.

01:09:32.919 --> 01:09:35.638
But the titles I remember for sure:

01:09:35.639 --> 01:09:38.338
Why? Why? Why? Why? Why?

01:09:38.339 --> 01:09:43.339
Wait for you, The 6th Summer, WAY 4 LUV.

01:09:43.890 --> 01:09:45.878
[Chat: Too catchy for exam season.]

01:09:45.879 --> 01:09:48.398
So those three—well, four.

01:09:48.399 --> 01:09:51.079
Those are the ones whose titles

01:09:51.080 --> 01:09:52.669
I know for sure.

01:09:52.679 --> 01:09:54.138
Uh…

01:09:54.139 --> 01:09:56.709
This is fun. Wait for you first?

01:09:56.719 --> 01:09:58.839
Should we watch the MV? You guys,

01:09:58.840 --> 01:10:00.439
I'll take recommendations.

01:10:00.440 --> 01:10:02.339
There's an Ideal Type World Cup, so…

01:10:04.430 --> 01:10:08.439
Do we do a PLAVE Song World Cup…

01:10:08.440 --> 01:10:12.270
I'm a little torn on what to do.

01:10:12.280 --> 01:10:15.149
Hold on. Live performances…

01:10:15.159 --> 01:10:17.229
Music videos? Oh, the ones with MVs.

01:10:17.239 --> 01:10:19.310
I wonder which songs

01:10:19.320 --> 01:10:20.990
have a music video.

01:10:21.000 --> 01:10:23.149
Let's do the Shorts World Cup later.

01:10:23.159 --> 01:10:24.830
We'll try that another time.

01:10:24.840 --> 01:10:27.590
[To chat] So, should I go in order?

01:10:27.600 --> 01:10:29.779
Should we just go through the songs in order?

01:10:29.780 --> 01:10:32.380
Starting with Wait for you.

01:10:39.000 --> 01:10:43.300
[Chat: A Song World Cup would take forever.
How about MVs and live stages?]

01:10:43.360 --> 01:10:45.320
I'll start on YouTube.

01:10:46.040 --> 01:10:47.270
Ja, let's see. Wait, wait.

01:10:47.280 --> 01:10:51.199
Wait. Ja, the screen too…

01:10:51.200 --> 01:10:54.520
I'll go fullscreen for this.

01:10:54.919 --> 01:10:58.519
Ah, the chat window. Hang on.

01:10:58.520 --> 01:10:59.783
I'll take the clock out.

01:11:00.659 --> 01:11:02.799
[Reading chat] “Try live stages.”

01:11:02.800 --> 01:11:04.759
Ten hours? We've got two days.

01:11:04.760 --> 01:11:07.470
We can keep watching till tomorrow.

01:11:07.690 --> 01:11:08.870
Uh…

01:11:10.620 --> 01:11:13.510
I will make myself a little bit shorter.

01:11:14.940 --> 01:11:16.810
I'm not the important part here.

01:11:17.640 --> 01:11:20.079
Should I hide the chat? But then…

01:11:20.080 --> 01:11:22.830
that's half the fun. This much is fine.

01:11:22.840 --> 01:11:24.029
I'll leave this much.

01:11:24.030 --> 01:11:26.460
Just this much.

01:11:30.280 --> 01:11:33.220
[Chat: No, we meant hide the chat! LOL]

01:11:33.239 --> 01:11:34.879
We're here to talk with each other

01:11:34.880 --> 01:11:37.790
as we watch. Ja. Oh, I…

01:11:37.800 --> 01:11:40.550
I feel weird. This might kill me. Ja,

01:11:40.560 --> 01:11:41.876
here we go. Wait for you.

01:11:43.900 --> 01:11:45.780
[Chat: I envy your first time.]

01:11:45.800 --> 01:11:48.178
You guys, there might be bits I really like.

01:11:48.179 --> 01:11:52.669
I'll pause to savor some of those. Yeah.

01:11:52.679 --> 01:11:55.709
Oh, it's my first time seeing the MV.

01:11:55.719 --> 01:11:58.638
I've only heard the song, so I'll try

01:11:58.639 --> 01:12:00.510
to play it all the way through first.

01:12:00.520 --> 01:12:03.950
Then we can go back

01:12:03.960 --> 01:12:06.470
to the parts I really liked. Whoa.

01:12:06.480 --> 01:12:09.019
Whoa, a whale! I'll turn the music up.

01:12:09.799 --> 01:12:12.830
Ja, hang on. Wait a minute.

01:12:12.840 --> 01:12:13.799
Ja…

01:12:13.800 --> 01:12:16.100
[Chat: Take your time! Pauses are fine.]

01:12:16.160 --> 01:12:18.390
When I do a Song World Cup…

01:12:18.400 --> 01:12:21.518
I want to listen properly.

01:12:21.519 --> 01:12:26.519
I'll get my headphones for music.

01:12:29.440 --> 01:12:31.400
Ja, earbuds out.

01:12:37.000 --> 01:12:40.800
[Chat: Look at our rookie PLLI,
coming prepared! LOL]

01:12:40.880 --> 01:12:42.638
I'm not missing a thing.

01:12:42.639 --> 01:12:45.510
Ja, from the top. Wait, though.

01:12:45.520 --> 01:12:47.079
Wait, isn't that the Dolphin Duo?

01:12:47.080 --> 01:12:48.279
Seriously? Also,

01:12:49.440 --> 01:12:52.110
tell me if the music's too loud

01:12:52.120 --> 01:12:56.649
or too quiet, okay?

01:12:56.650 --> 01:13:00.180
Whoa, wait. This was their debut song?!

01:13:02.910 --> 01:13:05.510
Their debut? Look at the quality!

01:13:05.520 --> 01:13:07.999
And this is from 2023!

01:13:12.159 --> 01:13:16.990
Whoa, that sound is insane.

01:13:17.000 --> 01:13:21.000
[Chat: Time to sing the PLLI anthem.]

01:13:21.180 --> 01:13:23.670
Should I turn on captions? Nah.

01:13:23.679 --> 01:13:25.279
Okay, I'm gonna focus on this.

01:13:25.280 --> 01:13:27.491
I'll focus on the video, not the captions.

01:13:29.000 --> 01:13:32.700
[Chat: Yes, this was their debut song.]

01:13:34.370 --> 01:13:36.170
They were doing this at debut?!

01:13:36.810 --> 01:13:39.670
Whoa, what? Even now, this looks wild.

01:13:46.030 --> 01:13:47.230
Whoa.

01:13:49.230 --> 01:13:51.650
Whoa, that gives me chills.

01:13:54.990 --> 01:13:57.020
How are they even…

01:13:58.060 --> 01:13:59.700
Yeah, their diction is great.

01:13:59.900 --> 01:14:01.800
And I've heard this song so often…

01:14:08.120 --> 01:14:12.050
[Chat: Their label's a tech company.
They're good at bringing this to life.]

01:14:20.810 --> 01:14:25.030
It feels like they're talking to people
who'll become fans someday.

01:14:26.120 --> 01:14:29.150
Like they're waiting for them.

01:14:30.080 --> 01:14:33.080
Like, we haven't met yet.

01:14:33.100 --> 01:14:34.680
Not yet. It's just that…

01:14:36.090 --> 01:14:39.040
you didn't know me yet. That's the feeling.

01:14:41.260 --> 01:14:42.660
Whoa.

01:14:45.840 --> 01:14:48.980
On the internet, or in all
these different worlds…

01:14:50.250 --> 01:14:52.930
Wait, are those Yataz?

01:14:55.610 --> 01:14:56.710
Or not?

01:14:59.610 --> 01:15:02.430
Right, that's exactly the vibe I get.

01:15:02.450 --> 01:15:04.670
They're going, “Hello, hello.”

01:15:05.630 --> 01:15:07.200
[To chat] Oh, it really is Yataz?

01:15:07.220 --> 01:15:08.620
This is so fun.

01:15:08.740 --> 01:15:12.150
[Chat: They've been waiting since debut.
How could you NOT become a fan?]

01:15:12.170 --> 01:15:14.830
Whoa, it's like…

01:15:16.470 --> 01:15:20.630
Honestly, I swear I've never seen this MV.

01:15:20.650 --> 01:15:23.400
I've seriously never seen it.

01:15:26.200 --> 01:15:27.630
But, like…

01:15:30.940 --> 01:15:32.270
Whoa.

01:15:35.500 --> 01:15:39.180
[Chat: This part always makes me tear up.]

01:15:40.340 --> 01:15:42.090
Ah, so…

01:15:42.100 --> 01:15:45.340
because you found us…

01:15:46.030 --> 01:15:48.950
we came together in the same place.

01:15:49.840 --> 01:15:51.430
And then…

01:15:57.100 --> 01:16:00.580
[Chat: The group dance always gives me chills.]

01:16:03.940 --> 01:16:05.180
Whoa.

01:16:07.910 --> 01:16:10.140
The dance is so damn good.

01:16:32.350 --> 01:16:34.250
Wait, is it over?

01:16:34.880 --> 01:16:37.250
What? Was that two minutes?

01:16:38.140 --> 01:16:39.860
It's 3 minutes and 55 seconds.

01:16:39.900 --> 01:16:42.020
Why not give us one more chorus?

01:16:43.050 --> 01:16:44.640
Huh? Whoa.

01:16:45.590 --> 01:16:48.000
I seriously don't get it. That just now…

01:16:48.010 --> 01:16:49.950
was four minutes?

01:16:50.020 --> 01:16:52.110
[Chat: Bamby and Hamin made the choreo.]

01:16:52.130 --> 01:16:53.940
They're in different worlds…

01:16:53.950 --> 01:16:56.530
scattered at first.

01:16:59.920 --> 01:17:01.320
Each on their own.

01:17:01.940 --> 01:17:03.350
Whoa.

01:17:06.870 --> 01:17:09.070
They each have their own world.

01:17:09.110 --> 01:17:13.490
[Chat: They come together from their own
worlds, and PLLI gather too.]

01:17:14.980 --> 01:17:17.660
I'll turn on the captions.

01:17:18.910 --> 01:17:21.400
Sorry. With songs like this…

01:17:21.410 --> 01:17:25.410
Even one song is hard to move on from.

01:17:26.880 --> 01:17:28.700
I said just a spoonful today…

01:17:28.720 --> 01:17:31.090
but I'm getting a ladle.

01:17:36.940 --> 01:17:40.520
I might not remember their names
right away, by the way.

01:17:40.960 --> 01:17:43.080
Oh, I'm talking to myself.

01:17:45.640 --> 01:17:47.680
[Reading chat] “MV first, then the stage?”

01:17:47.690 --> 01:17:48.650
Nice.

01:17:48.670 --> 01:17:52.440
I had to see this to really get the lore.

01:17:52.460 --> 01:17:54.100
Just seeing it like this…

01:18:02.120 --> 01:18:05.220
This is my first time really reading the lyrics.

01:18:08.100 --> 01:18:12.150
[Chat: Forget the ladle. You'll be eating
straight from the pot. LOL]

01:18:18.040 --> 01:18:20.910
Oh, Bamby and Eunho are in the same world.

01:18:20.920 --> 01:18:23.090
That's why they're Yataz.

01:18:30.000 --> 01:18:33.550
[Chat: Now I'm starting to wonder
who your bias will be.]

01:18:42.170 --> 01:18:46.340
Ja—whoa. Hang on. This is killing me.

01:18:47.590 --> 01:18:50.410
Wait, did I turn that thing off earlier?

01:18:50.860 --> 01:18:52.130
Why is it so…

01:18:52.780 --> 01:18:55.180
I mean, the quality…

01:19:02.910 --> 01:19:04.740
Ya! Ta! [Get on!]

01:19:06.640 --> 01:19:08.980
This is really their debut video?

01:19:09.000 --> 01:19:10.580
[Reading chat] “Your bias?”

01:19:10.600 --> 01:19:12.790
I don't have a bias yet.

01:19:16.950 --> 01:19:20.010
But let's keep watching for now.

01:19:33.800 --> 01:19:36.060
Did his ear just get rubbed raw?

01:19:36.080 --> 01:19:37.678
Bamby?

01:19:37.679 --> 01:19:39.750
See? He's touching his ear. It hurts!

01:19:39.760 --> 01:19:42.200
It rubbed his ear. Ouch.

01:19:42.960 --> 01:19:45.950
And he still told him to hop on!

01:19:52.840 --> 01:19:55.700
Whoa, the rap! I like this.

01:19:59.939 --> 01:20:02.629
It's smooth, like 3D…

01:20:02.630 --> 01:20:03.850
and then,

01:20:04.010 --> 01:20:08.090
this part suddenly turns 2D.

01:20:08.150 --> 01:20:14.300
They hit refresh, right? They refreshed it.

01:20:18.750 --> 01:20:23.300
People came in and started watching…

01:20:24.320 --> 01:20:26.470
So…

01:20:26.480 --> 01:20:28.709
Whoa, a refresh. This is insane.

01:20:28.719 --> 01:20:31.510
So that's kind of what it means…

01:20:31.520 --> 01:20:36.520
[Reading chat] “That's the developer's hand?”

01:20:40.620 --> 01:20:44.090
[Chat: F5 might be the Run key
in the software they're using.]

01:20:44.120 --> 01:20:46.830
It's like refreshing the whole world.

01:20:46.840 --> 01:20:48.314
And in that refreshed world,

01:20:48.719 --> 01:20:53.830
that's where they meet, right?

01:20:53.900 --> 01:20:56.498
[Chat: Wow, you caught that right away.]

01:20:56.499 --> 01:21:01.499
Then they show it for the first time.

01:21:05.720 --> 01:21:09.220
[Chat: This is Asterum.]

01:21:09.239 --> 01:21:12.229
Oh, in the lore, the place they gather…

01:21:12.239 --> 01:21:13.289
that's Asterum?

01:21:14.139 --> 01:21:16.149
I don't know how.

01:21:16.159 --> 01:21:21.159
It's fine, it's fine.

01:21:22.570 --> 01:21:24.390
[Reading chat] “You've got good taste.”

01:21:24.400 --> 01:21:26.499
I like getting a taste like this.

01:21:27.520 --> 01:21:29.718
And getting to talk it through

01:21:29.719 --> 01:21:33.229
with you guys, too.

01:21:38.960 --> 01:21:42.098
They went from talking to themselves
to there being two of them…

01:21:42.099 --> 01:21:43.579
and then there were five.

01:21:49.050 --> 01:21:50.980
So we're on Earth, looking at…

01:21:51.000 --> 01:21:53.358
Asterum. Is that how it works?

01:21:53.359 --> 01:21:55.919
Like, from over there…

01:21:55.920 --> 01:21:57.319
they see us. And we see them.

01:21:57.320 --> 01:22:00.990
Is that it? Damn, that's deep.

01:22:01.000 --> 01:22:02.940
[Chat: Looking at Terra, where PLLI are.]

01:22:03.299 --> 01:22:06.258
[Reading chat] “So PLAVE are aliens?”

01:22:06.259 --> 01:22:08.719
Aliens like that are more than welcome.

01:22:09.560 --> 01:22:11.198
Oh, and something I was trying

01:22:11.199 --> 01:22:14.229
to say earlier about PLAVE's songs.

01:22:14.239 --> 01:22:16.859
How do I put it? All five voices…

01:22:17.400 --> 01:22:18.938
sound like one person singing.

01:22:18.939 --> 01:22:20.898
They blend so well. I mean…

01:22:20.899 --> 01:22:23.390
they each have their own sound,

01:22:23.400 --> 01:22:25.198
but when all five sing, it's so smooth.

01:22:25.199 --> 01:22:27.439
It's almost soothing.

01:22:27.440 --> 01:22:30.959
That's why I put on my PLAVE playlist

01:22:30.960 --> 01:22:32.750
and just let it play.

01:22:32.760 --> 01:22:37.430
That's why I liked them. Yeah.

01:22:37.440 --> 01:22:38.490
This is so good.

01:22:40.000 --> 01:22:41.158
Oh, this is delicious.

01:22:41.959 --> 01:22:44.378
Hang on. Now that I've seen the MV,

01:22:44.379 --> 01:22:46.279
let's watch Wait for you

01:22:46.639 --> 01:22:48.878
live.

01:22:48.879 --> 01:22:50.829
Oh, right. Yeah.

01:22:50.830 --> 01:22:52.920
[Chat: Oh, a real foodie!]

01:22:53.120 --> 01:22:55.898
Which one should I watch?

01:22:55.899 --> 01:23:00.350
Which one? Should I play the first one?

01:23:00.619 --> 01:23:05.600
4.36 million views? Oh, what's this?

01:23:06.620 --> 01:23:08.550
MBC. [Show! Music Core]

01:23:09.320 --> 01:23:10.929
Oh, that's insane.

01:23:10.930 --> 01:23:14.510
[On-screen: Stage footage cut
for broadcaster copyright reasons.]

01:23:14.530 --> 01:23:16.849
This is delicious.

01:23:16.850 --> 01:23:19.430
This is way better than I imagined.

01:23:20.080 --> 01:23:21.870
Hey, you guys, why have you been

01:23:21.880 --> 01:23:24.091
keeping all this good stuff to yourselves?

01:23:24.920 --> 01:23:27.500
That's GOAT-tier.

01:23:27.719 --> 01:23:30.950
It'll be fun to look up

01:23:30.960 --> 01:23:34.470
the choreo for each song, too. Ja, next…

01:23:34.480 --> 01:23:36.322
I want to watch the songs in order.

01:23:37.039 --> 01:23:39.479
Ja, for now, I'll hold off on the stages

01:23:39.480 --> 01:23:41.578
and get through all the MVs first.

01:23:41.579 --> 01:23:43.599
Am I ever finishing this today?

01:23:44.480 --> 01:23:47.879
I'm not sleeping tonight. Wait for you is second?

01:23:47.880 --> 01:23:49.250
Oh, they're sorted by views.

01:23:53.500 --> 01:23:56.350
I should start with the March 12 release.

01:23:56.400 --> 01:23:58.950
Pixel World.

01:24:00.070 --> 01:24:02.420
[Chat: That list is missing the B-sides.]

01:24:02.440 --> 01:24:06.500
[Chat: Why? is next for stages,
The 6th Summer for MVs.]

01:24:12.210 --> 01:24:14.380
Does Pixel World only have an audio track?

01:24:14.400 --> 01:24:16.930
[Chat: Yep, just the song.]

01:24:17.500 --> 01:24:20.000
But they have way more songs, right?

01:24:22.460 --> 01:24:24.460
Right, this isn't about me…

01:24:24.470 --> 01:24:25.770
…but I'll make myself

01:24:25.780 --> 01:24:28.050
a little larger since it's my own stream.

01:24:32.850 --> 01:24:34.320
[Reading chat] “A lyric video?”

01:24:34.400 --> 01:24:37.220
[Reading chat] “The live version is better?”

01:24:37.560 --> 01:24:40.250
I want to give this one a try, too.

01:24:45.280 --> 01:24:47.270
Should I go in order of views?

01:24:47.280 --> 01:24:48.859
But there's a story to follow.

01:24:49.719 --> 01:24:52.298
Oh, hi, hi! Glad you're here.

01:24:52.299 --> 01:24:53.349
Good evening.

01:24:53.739 --> 01:24:56.109
A lyric video? Hang on. Where is it?

01:24:56.119 --> 01:24:59.590
Lyric video…

01:24:59.610 --> 01:25:01.260
Only title tracks got MVs?

01:25:01.280 --> 01:25:03.299
I'll dig into the title tracks first.

01:25:04.719 --> 01:25:09.719
Hang on. What's the lyric video?

01:25:11.839 --> 01:25:13.539
“Music videos in order…”

01:25:15.000 --> 01:25:18.290
[Chat: Look up the B-sides
and digital singles separately.]

01:25:18.450 --> 01:25:20.160
Whoa, what's this?

01:25:32.980 --> 01:25:34.500
Blip?

01:25:40.280 --> 01:25:42.430
I bet there are plenty of guy PLLI, too.

01:25:42.440 --> 01:25:47.440
Hang on.

01:25:51.739 --> 01:25:56.250
The order… Oh, ChatGPT!

01:25:57.810 --> 01:26:01.550
Ja… I should just ask.

01:26:01.600 --> 01:26:03.430
Ja, so, PLAVE…

01:26:03.440 --> 01:26:06.830
I'm doing a livestream

01:26:06.840 --> 01:26:09.709
where I'm getting to know PLAVE.

01:26:09.719 --> 01:26:12.109
Can you list their music videos

01:26:12.119 --> 01:26:14.330
in release order?

01:26:16.400 --> 01:26:17.950
[Laughs]

01:26:17.990 --> 01:26:21.800
[Chat: Why look it up when we're right here?]

01:26:21.840 --> 01:26:24.399
No, it's just that

01:26:24.400 --> 01:26:26.070
I didn't want to bug you guys

01:26:26.080 --> 01:26:29.839
and figured it'd be quicker. Oh! Thank you.

01:26:29.840 --> 01:26:34.019
You were so quick! I was just trying to… Wait.

01:26:35.080 --> 01:26:36.950
Oh!

01:26:36.960 --> 01:26:39.338
[Reading chat] “Just ask us?” Oh, sorry!

01:26:39.339 --> 01:26:41.378
Sorry! I'll ask you guys.

01:26:41.379 --> 01:26:43.179
I'll ask you.

01:26:45.630 --> 01:26:47.780
Sorry!

01:26:48.600 --> 01:26:50.990
Ja…

01:26:51.000 --> 01:26:52.474
I've got good people to ask.

01:26:54.360 --> 01:26:56.600
Ja, so if I go here…

01:26:56.640 --> 01:27:00.170
[Chat: He asked GPT instead of us. LOL]

01:27:00.200 --> 01:27:02.450
There's so much to watch!

01:27:02.679 --> 01:27:05.299
Hang on.

01:27:05.300 --> 01:27:09.249
So the next song is…

01:27:09.250 --> 01:27:11.050
Why?

01:27:11.120 --> 01:27:15.700
[Chat: PLLI know PLAVE better than GPT. LOL]

01:27:16.790 --> 01:27:19.400
Oh, you mean “Why?”

01:27:21.920 --> 01:27:25.178
That's a song. There's a Music Core stage?

01:27:25.179 --> 01:27:26.839
Oh, really?

01:27:26.870 --> 01:27:28.500
[Chat: Try the third video!]

01:27:28.520 --> 01:27:31.669
The third one?

01:27:31.679 --> 01:27:33.990
I'll watch this one, too.

01:27:34.000 --> 01:27:34.999
Stage clips too.

01:27:39.140 --> 01:27:42.810
I'll make myself smaller now
that we're watching the video.

01:27:53.400 --> 01:27:54.550
Oh!

01:27:57.840 --> 01:27:58.810
Oh!

01:27:58.820 --> 01:28:00.730
Whoa, whoa! What was that?

01:28:02.350 --> 01:28:04.090
Whoa, that dance!

01:28:13.150 --> 01:28:16.750
[Chat: This is a live performance.]

01:28:19.080 --> 01:28:20.890
Oooh!

01:28:28.020 --> 01:28:30.700
Oh, I love that transition in the middle.

01:28:32.950 --> 01:28:34.050
Wow.

01:28:34.690 --> 01:28:35.960
Wow.

01:28:37.580 --> 01:28:39.810
Whoa, what was that?

01:28:39.820 --> 01:28:42.200
How is that falsetto so good?

01:28:42.220 --> 01:28:43.690
Let's go!

01:28:53.150 --> 01:28:56.280
[Chat: The falsetto really is amazing.]

01:28:57.020 --> 01:28:59.450
Oh, is he covering his eyes?

01:29:00.900 --> 01:29:02.740
Ay, ay!

01:29:09.790 --> 01:29:11.650
Whoa, what was that?

01:29:12.780 --> 01:29:14.470
Wait, what?

01:29:16.150 --> 01:29:17.260
Noah-hyung!

01:29:17.280 --> 01:29:18.910
He's actually younger than me,

01:29:18.920 --> 01:29:21.950
but if he's that handsome, he's my hyung.

01:29:29.150 --> 01:29:30.580
[Laughs]

01:29:35.120 --> 01:29:38.300
[Chat: The choreo is so cute.]

